on my bed in the cell?

253
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:17,492
I'd better find a place to write it down.

254
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,920
What was I doing just now?

255
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,717
I know I came back to
the cell for something.

256
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:31,630
What was it?

257
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:35,580
Come on, think.

258
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:40,837
It had to be at least important
enough to take the trouble.

259
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:41,750
Jolyne!

260
00:16:41,833 --> 00:16:42,697
That's my lunch you're eating!

261
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:43,898
Drop that fork now!

262
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:45,877
Oh man, it's almost gone!

263
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:48,997
That was my favorite cheese
penne and you snarfed it all!

264
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:49,910
Dumbass!

265
00:16:49,993 --> 00:16:53,113
You put your own meal ticket
in your pocket this morning!

266
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:57,930
Sorry.

267
00:16:58,013 --> 00:17:00,697
I'll use this to go get you
a replacement meal then.

268
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:02,192
It's fine really, don't.

269
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:05,877
How about you just give me your meal
ticket and I'll go get it myself.

270
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:06,790
Thank you.

271
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:09,497
And maybe you should write
it down somewhere this time.

272
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:13,140
I gave my meal ticket to Guaz,
I didn't lose it. My bad.

273
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:21,240
Who's this? A user?

274
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:23,636
That can only mean that it's a stand.

275
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,460
Oh, that's right.

276
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:27,169
I have to go find Emporio.

277
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:30,286
I was trying to escape
from the isolated cell.

278
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:33,417
And I was probably with
Emporio at the time.

279
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:35,147
That's the only explanation.

280
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,457
I bet he knows something
about it that can help me.

281
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:40,080
He knows I want to escape.

282
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:43,300
Hey, we have a big problem.

283
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:45,077
There's no more mustard in here.

284
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,020
It's empty!

285
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:47,640
How about a new one?

286
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:51,370
This again?

287
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:54,209
Do they serve the same
crap every day here?

288
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:56,566
I'm not even all that hungry.

289
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,837
I'll just eat the cheese
penny, that's good.

290
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:00,840
Hey Jolene, mind if I sit down?

291
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:10,180
I'll take that as a yes.

292
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:13,272
I stepped on a fucking cockroach earlier.

293
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,602
Now there's dead bug on my shoes

294
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:18,960
Who is this woman so weird?

295
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:24,920
She obviously knows who I am tall
blonde split ends cut out stockings

296
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,017
You asshole?

297
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,517
The hell are you doing to my lunch?

298
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:31,012
This needs some mustard!

299
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:34,820
Maybe a little ketchup to?

300
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,478
Dressing would be the perfect touch!

301
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,437
That's delicious!

302
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:51,497
Thanks a lot!

303
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:55,117
You look so familiar! What's your name?

304
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,030
Oh no!

305
00:18:56,113 --> 00:18:57,497
I'm so sorry! Jolene!

306
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:58,817
Look what a mess I've made!

307
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:00,097
Please let me clean it up!

308
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,010
Oh!

309
00:19:01,093 --> 00:19:01,923
It got all over your arm too!

310
00:19:02,006 --> 00:19:02,897
It's really dirty!

311
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,837
I'm just gonna wipe away all that grunge!

312
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:05,750
Scrubby!

313
00:19:05,833 --> 00:19:06,663
Scrub!

314
00:19:06,746 --> 00:19:09,080
There we go! All cleaned! Stand up!

315
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,517
Isn't that better now?

316
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,659
Let me see inside that pocket, too.

317
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:19,711
I'll just leave that for you to look over.

318
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:21,820
Jailhouse lock.

319
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,197
Anyone who, while trying to escape,

320
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:28,797
touches the bars my stands in will only be
able to remember three things at a time,

321
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:29,710
sadly.

322
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:31,980
A life of threes appears simple,

323
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:36,102
but it's actually more difficult
than losing all of your memories.

324
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:38,220
You will continuously repeat,

325
00:19:38,700 --> 00:19:41,897
experience, and be painfully reminded
that everything you do is useless.

326
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:45,380
An arduous feedback loop that
slowly erodes your spirit.

327
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:49,462
Eventually, it'll even
drain your will to escape.

328
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,197
It might feel something like paralysis,

329
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:57,045
but really, that's your appropriate
punishment for trying to break out of prison.

330
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,960
I know I need something, but what?

331
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:04,090
What's important?

332
00:20:04,173 --> 00:20:06,061
What's something I cannot forget?

333
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:09,497
What do I need to break
through this situation?

334
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:10,820
Just one thing!

335
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,260
That's all I need!

336
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:14,400
I gotta remember it.

337
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:17,758
Cause if I can't do that
now, I'll forget it forever!

338
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,020
One goddamn thing.

339
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,620
But what matters most is...

340
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:31,680
This, this is all I need.

341
00:20:32,020 --> 00:20:33,726
I'll leave room for one more.

342
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,788
Now it's down to these two.

343
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:38,040
These two are the only ones I need.

344
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:40,200
I can 86 the rest myself.

345
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:43,873
And get back to my goal of
breaking the fuck out of here!

346
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:48,510
I...

347
00:20:48,593 --> 00:20:49,500
I spilled my water!

348
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:51,020
This is really bad!

349
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:54,820
I'm being electrocuted.

350
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:57,456
I have to pull the plug before I die.

351
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,117
Otherwise, I...

352
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:04,980
I can't leave this room through that exit
and meet Jolene like I'm supposed to.

353
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:10,320
I have something important to tell
Jolene. I gotta go. She needs me.

354
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:13,228
No matter what happens,
I can't forget that.

355
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:16,154
I have to get out of this room quickly.

356
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,090
Oh, no.

357
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:24,560
I spilled my water.

358
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:28,900
I have to pull the plug before I die.

359
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:32,540
I'm being electrocuted.

360
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:39,960
Otherwise, I can't leave this room
through that exit and meet Jolene.

361
00:21:44,740 --> 00:21:46,460
I won't be able to see her.

362
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:49,880
Wait a minute.

363
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:52,080
I have to go see Emporio?

364
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:57,237
I remember seeing something like that on
Jolene's arm right before I wiped it off.

365
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:59,791
I suppose I'll have to confirm it, though.

366
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:02,277
Still, no one's escaping from here.

367
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,889
it's an airtight fortress.

368
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:35,640
My head is filled with hope.

369
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:43,700
Of some place other than here.

370
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:50,100
Although you think I smile.

371
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:55,220
Inside and all the while.

372
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:03,400
I'm wondering about my destiny.

373
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:07,857
I'm thinking

374
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:13,137
about all

375
00:23:13,220 --> 00:23:19,380
the things I'd like to do?

376
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,997
In my life,

377
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:31,637
I'm a dreamer,

378
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:34,377
a distant dreamer,

379
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:38,177
dreaming far

380
00:23:38,260 --> 00:23:44,420
away from today.

381
00:23:51,860 --> 00:23:52,690
Thank you.

382
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:21,200
Thank you.
